# expect: 2000000000
# expect: 3000000000
# expect: 4000000000
# expect: ok
# `for $stream [body]` — the block iterates the stream, binding $it to each
# element. Over a wide i64 stream the binding narrows to i64, so the element is
# handed over wide and wide arithmetic in the body works on it directly. Values
# past INT32_MAX guard against tag confusion at the binding boundary. (The
# transform mapper is still an inline closure — HOFs keep closures.)
proc main [] [
  for [transform [range 1 4] [\ $* $it 1000000000]] [print [+ $it 1000000000]]
  print "ok"                        # prints 2e9, 3e9, 4e9
]
main
